      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "1. Let the common difference of the arithmetic sequence be \\(-1\\).\n2. The fifth term of the arithmetic sequence is the sum of the first four terms plus the fifth term itself, that is \\(a_5 = a_1 + 4d\\).\n3. So, we can express the fifth term as \\(11 = a_1 + 4(-1)\\).\n4. Solving for \\(a_1\\):\n\\begin{align*}\n11 &= a_1 - 4 \\\\\na_1 &= 11 + 4 \\\\\na_1 &= 15\n\\end{align*}\n5. So, the first term is \\(a_1\\) and the second term is \\(a_1 + d\\), i.e., \\(15\\).\n6. Calculating the product, we get:\n\\begin{align*}\na_1 \\cdot a_2 &= 15 \\cdot (15 - 1) \\\\\n&= 15 \\cdot 14 \\\\\n&= 210\n\\end{align*}\n\nHence, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{210}\\)",
